This empty file switches GitHub Pages OUT of Jekyll and makes it serve the
repository as plain static files.

Why it exists — a real failure, not a precaution:
  Three deployments in a row errored with a 0ms duration (builds #330, #331,
  #332 on 2026-10-14) while the owner kept seeing Build v257 and reported that
  the breakage and the tips opening "did not change". The code was on main the
  whole time; it was never published.

  This project is plain HTML/JS with no Jekyll content at all, yet Jekyll was
  parsing every file as a Liquid template — including admin.html, which is
  2.4 MB. Successful builds already took 35 to 140 seconds for that reason
  alone, and admin.html carries a JSDoc comment reading `@returns {{mandoob:
  string, employee: string}}`, which Liquid reads as template syntax.

  With this file present the build is a file copy: no Liquid, no template
  parsing, far faster, and nothing in the source can break the deployment by
  looking like a template.

⚠ Do not delete it. And do not merge two pull requests within a few minutes of
  each other: each merge starts a deployment that CANCELS the one before it, so
  the site stays on the older version while the newest merge looks done.
